  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 19 February 2025, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 19 February 205 and numbered 23120-PP-001, 23120_PP_100 Rev01, 23120_PP_101 Rev01, 23120_PP_102 Rev01, 23120_PP_103 Rev01, 23120_PP_300 Rev01, 23120_PP_301 Rev01, 23120_PP_302 Rev01, 23120_PP_303 Rev01, 23120_PP_304 Rev01, 23120_PP_305 Rev01, 23120_PP_200 Rev01, 23120_PP_201 Rev01, 23120_PP_202 Rev01, 23120_PP_203 Rev01was lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 because:\r\n\r\nThe proposed works described in the application would not constitute \"development\" for the purposes of Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended), as they would not involve a material change in the use of land and/or operational development. As such, the proposal would be considered lawful under section 191 or 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act (as amended)."
